{:edb/db-before-t 1867 :edb/db-after-t 1868 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535180 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:50:28.234Z" 13194139535180 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335830 13194139535180 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335837 13194139535180 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335844 13194139535180 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335851 13194139535180 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335854 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335831 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1089 "q-106515" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/999d1d14a31f9619306efe6b1c2ebc6e900a52bf4e2d2edd7230e7dd7c9b25b9.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm 2x.$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1113 #uuid "57a70c61-ca1c-517f-b49f-a1db49c2f10a" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335830 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(1,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm 2x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\frac{b}{1} & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335832 13194139535180 true] [17592186335831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335833 13194