nce/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/b570ce72a87d7583a230ea1c863656f982c7fefeb546295d41429876cc823837.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x.$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335837 1113 #uuid "731d98b7-b827-5e98-bc4b-a4e46aa03b9e" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335837 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(2,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=2.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{b}{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335839 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335840 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335841 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335842 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335843 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1041 "selection" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335839 13194139535180 true] [17592186335838 1110 #uuid "90b838b8-e502-5a6e-b66a-3e1a9a75cd86" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335839 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335839 1111 #uuid "4472205c-c0c7-5cf9-8946-6e05f17bf732" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335840 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335840 1111 #uuid "7679a998-15be-54ad-a2e3-ca88f39fdd7a" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335841 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335841 1111 #uuid "48bb799a-2e2a-5921-b3c8-961cc33efbe0" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335842 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335842 1111 #uuid "0b09fed6-9bf8-522c-a457-2f7e4f4f1d06" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335843 1034 "x=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335843 1111 #uuid "ba06d81e-e540-5865-a9f8-3d5727309dc4" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335845 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1089 "q-106524" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1113 #uuid "7c274a2a-ce8f-57fe-a73e-45cba23684ad" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335844 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335846 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335847 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335848 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335849 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335850 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1041 "selection" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335848 13194139535180 true] [17592186335845 1110 #uuid "b3f250da-1e15-5918-96f9-0b43d8fd1ada" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335846 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335846 1111 #uuid "b8043a04-4ad9-5068-ab03-9534e2632810" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335847 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335847 1111 #uuid "5b8a8c4a-0cf9-556e-88c1-cb015567883e" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335848 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335848 1111 #uuid "f577bed4-fd4a-50cc-81ae-9571a81b010f" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335849 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335849 1111 #uuid "06837e4a-132e-5d28-8d49-2cb8e24af5e7" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335850 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335850 1111 #uuid "94369efc-c634-5d2d-80a4-2f8a3d5ebe95" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335852 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1089 "q-325941" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=10\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1113 #uuid "4a34c59e-1cd9-5fb4-9616-c68d076c6f17" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335851 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{10} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{100} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335853 13194139535180 true] [17592186335852 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535180 true] [17592186335852 1041 "field-1" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335852 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335853 13194139535180 true] [17592186335852 1110 #uuid "dc2677a1-f592-567d-a53c-95d35518b2b5" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335853 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{100}-\\frac{y^2}{9}" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535180 true] [17592186335853 1111 #uuid "6aecc25a-0f60-5138-81de-6ca15b6da3fb" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335855 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1089 "q-89347" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1113 #uuid "698299c1-e40e-528b-a38d-66f6a77ea0e0" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335854 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" 13194139535180 true] [17592186335855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335856 13194139535180 true] [17592186335855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335857 13194139535180 true] [17592186335855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335858 13194139535